[2026-03-29 23:44:29] Expanding SCB coverage to the next natural targets and correcting the reset helper after a TM4C129X plus Cortex-M4 spec cross-check.
- Production sources under review:
  - TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/Core/SCB/Driver/xSource/SCB_SysReset.c
  - TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/Core/SCB/Driver/Traps/xSource/SCB_DivisionTrap.c
  - TM4C129E_DriverLib/xDriver_MCU/Core/SCB/Driver/Traps/xSource/SCB_UnalignTrap.c
- Documentation basis reviewed from extracted manuals:
  - Cortex-M4 AIRCR requires keyed writes with `VECTKEY = 0x5FA`.
  - Cortex-M4 marks `VECTRESET` debug-reserved and requires `0` unless the implementation defines its use.
  - TM4C129X documents `SYSRESREQ` for full microcontroller reset and `VECTRESET` for core-only reset.
  - CCR `DIV_0_TRP` and `UNALIGN_TRP` semantics match the existing wrapper intent.
- Production defect found and corrected in `SCB_SysReset.c`:
  - the debug reset path used an incorrect AIRCR mask/value composition
  - both reset helpers entered the fallback no-op loop even when the write primitive reported an error
- Planned host targets:
  - SCB_SysReset_Test
  - SCB_DivisionTrap_Test
  - SCB_UnalignTrap_Test